  "discovery": {
    "note": "Discovery reads open feeds where almost nothing is relevant. Two lessons from live runs. First, the scoring legs are far too broad here: api, automation and rendering match every backend job. Second, and the reason for title_patterns: generative ai is boilerplate in ordinary software ads now, so a Java Engineer and an IT Operations Analyst both name it. In the run of 2026-09-02 every false positive had a non-creative job title and every real hit had a creative one, so the title carries the decision. A posting with an odd title still gets in on two distinct strong craft terms, which is how a real role at a real studio survives a title nobody standardized.",
